# Tokenizer cases that silksurf_html::Tokenizer does not yet reproduce. Each
# line records a known gap so a regression and a repair are both visible as a
# diff against this file; HTML5LIB_FAIL_ON_XPASS=1 promotes a newly passing
# case to a hard failure.
#
# This tokenizer serves tooling, not page loads: wpt_runner and the CSS harness
# use it to lift <style> contents out of markup. Production HTML parsing runs
# on html5ever through parse_html, measured by
# html5lib-tree-construction.expectations.
#
# Two mechanisms account for 3464 of the 3621 entries:
#
#   named character references (2226 in namedEntities, 57 in entities) --
#   the tokenizer emits the source text of a reference rather than the
#   character it names, so "&AElig" stays literal instead of resolving to the
#   character U+00C6. WHATWG HTML tokenization requires the longest-match
#   named-reference table, which lib.rs does not carry.
#
#   test3 permutations (1238) -- test3 walks tag, attribute, and markup
#   openings through every insertion point. The State enum in lib.rs carries 8
#   states against roughly 80 in the standard, so the permutations that need a
#   state this tokenizer lacks resolve to the wrong token boundary.
#
# The remainder are led by DOCTYPE name handling: the standard ASCII-lowercases
# a DOCTYPE name, and this tokenizer preserves source case.

